      "outputTokens": 1300,
      "costUsd": 0.011779,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended here, with F of x equals x squared over nine. Let's give it a meaning. A parcel tracker says your delivery will come between nine and twelve. X is the arrival time in hours after nine, and F of x is the chance the parcel has arrived by then. F climbs slowly near zero, and steeply near three. Compare two strips of the same width, a tenth of an hour. From zero point five to zero point six, F only rises by about zero point zero one two. From two point five to two point six, it rises by about zero point zero five seven. So the same width holds almost five times as much probability near two point five. Steep means the arrival times are packed closely. So how do we measure that packing?"
    },
    {
