      "inputTokens": 125,
      "outputTokens": 984,
      "costUsd": 0.0089185,
      "pronunciationText": "So for a density, probability is area. For the density models we use, F is a primitive of f, so the area under f from c to d is F of d minus F of c. That's exactly the probability that X is between c and d. For the parcel, the area under two x over nine from one to two is four ninths minus one ninth, which is one third. That's the chance it arrives between ten and eleven, the same one third last video found from F. And since single values carry no probability, the ends of the interval still don't matter."
    },
