      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 927,
      "costUsd": 0.008404,
      "pronunciationText": "Every density has two properties. First, f of x is never negative, because F never decreases, so its gradient can't be below zero. Second, the total area under f is one, because that's all of the probability. If X lives on an interval from a to b, the integral from a to b is one. If X can be any real number, the integral from minus infinity to infinity is one. Check two x over nine. It's never negative from zero to three, and its area is a triangle, half of three times two thirds, which is one."
