      "inputTokens": 117,
      "outputTokens": 890,
      "costUsd": 0.0080685,
      "pronunciationText": "These two properties solve problems. A second courier's arrival time, X hours after eight, has density k times four minus x, for x from zero to four, and zero elsewhere. Their stop is early on the route, so early arrivals are most likely. Find k. The total area must be one. The graph is a triangle with base four and height four k, so its area is eight k. Integrating gives the same answer. So eight k equals one, and k is one eighth. It has to be positive, because a density can't be negative."
