      "inputTokens": 124,
      "outputTokens": 897,
      "costUsd": 0.008135,
      "pronunciationText": "We can also build F from f. F of x is the area under f from the start of the domain up to x. So F of x is the integral from zero to x of f of t, d t. The letter t is a dummy variable, because x is already the upper limit. Here, that gives eight x minus x squared, over sixteen, for x from zero to four. Check the ends. F of zero is zero, and F of four is thirty two minus sixteen, over sixteen, which is one. And F of one is seven sixteenths, the area we just found."
