      "inputTokens": 113,
      "outputTokens": 885,
      "costUsd": 0.008021499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Going the other way takes one step. Differentiate. A variable has F of x equals x squared times three minus x, over four, for x from zero to two. First check the ends. F of zero is zero, and F of two is four times one, over four, which is one. Expand it, and differentiate. The density is three x times two minus x, over four. Both factors are positive between zero and two, so f is never negative. And f is zero elsewhere, because the flat pieces of F have gradient zero."
