      "inputTokens": 92,
      "outputTokens": 656,
      "costUsd": 0.00595,
      "pronunciationText": "The total area is k times x squared over two plus x, from zero to two, which is four k. So k is one quarter. Then the probability that X is more than one is the integral from one to two of x plus one, over four. That's one quarter of four minus one and a half, which is five eighths. Three quarters is wrong. That's the height of f at two, not an area."
