      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 77,
      "outputTokens": 586,
      "costUsd": 0.0053125,
      "pronunciationText": "Differentiate the middle piece. Four minus two x, over four, is two minus x, over two, for x from zero to two. It's never negative there. Outside that interval, f is zero, because the flat pieces of F have gradient zero. Saying f is one for x above two is wrong. The derivative of a constant is zero, not one."
